# v16 verification log (2026-09-02)

External review follow-ups applied on top of v15:

1. Saved independent English runs synchronized to unified difficulty labels
   - `scripts/compute_unified_difficulty.py --apply` now also rewrites
     `evaluation/independent_en_run{1,2,3}.json`:
     * `results[].difficulty` updated from `independent_en_dataset.jsonl`
       (Easy 13 / Medium 8 / Hard 4 / Very Hard 0)
     * top-level `by_difficulty` recomputed from the updated labels and the
       unchanged per-query recalls
     * provenance note added: difficulty labels updated post hoc from the
       unified structural-complexity score; model outputs unchanged
   - Immutability check: for each run, every per-query field except
     `difficulty` is byte-identical to the v15 values (SQL, recall,
     latency, etc. unchanged). Only `results[].difficulty`,
     `by_difficulty`, and `provenance` changed.

2. Paired language test replaced by an exhaustive sign-permutation test
   - `scripts/compute_language_stats.py` now enumerates all 2^13 = 8192
     sign assignments of the midranks of |diff| (ties handled by midranks)
     and reports the two-sided p-value of the Wilcoxon signed-rank
     statistic under this exact permutation null:
       p = 1580/8192 = 0.193 (13 non-zero pairs)
   - This is SciPy-version independent (no reliance on method="auto").
   - Bootstrap 95% CI unchanged: [-5.8, +1.6] pp (seed 20260602,
     100,000 resamples). Mean diff unchanged: -2.0 pp.

3. Other Wilcoxon calls pinned to method="exact"
   - `scripts/eval_ablation_multirun.py`, `scripts/recompute_significance.py`
     now pass method="exact" explicitly (SciPy "auto" can select different
     methods across versions). Recomputed exact p-values match the stored
     paper values: no_fewshot 4.513e-12, no_dict 1.049e-04,
     no_reranker 1.953e-02, no_graph 1.484e-01, no_nbest 8.125e-01,
     no_guard 1.000.

4. Manuscript (stam-m_ja.tex)
   - p=0.216 -> exhaustive sign-permutation p=0.193 (both occurrences).
   - Footnote: stratified difference now attributed "mainly" to
